{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nDuring the F07 documentation-link validation run, the full test suite failed while a fixture created a ticket in an isolated temporary store. `src/rebar/_store/event_commit_git.py` terminated `git commit` after the 30-second `_GIT_TIMEOUT`. The completion-attestation behavior under test did not run. The exact node passed alone in 55.48 seconds.\n\nClosed ticket `moldavite-evasive-elephant` classifies the earlier occurrence as runner I/O contention during a long test job and directs maintainers to track a recurrence separately. Closed ticket `royal-weariless-zebrafish` addresses store-lock acquisition before the write body. It does not address a timeout after acquisition while `git commit` is running.\n\n## Plan\n- Reproduce the timeout under controlled concurrent temporary-store writes and capture subprocess timing.\n- Distinguish host I/O contention from incorrect timeout or fixture behavior.\n- Correct the proven failure class without retrying an unexplained intermittent failure.\n- Add focused regression coverage for the confirmed mechanism.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The root cause is demonstrated with repeatable evidence.\n- [ ] A regression test fails for the confirmed mechanism before the fix.\n- [ ] The fix addresses the failure class rather than one observed run.\n- [ ] Focused store and lifecycle tests pass.\n- [ ] The ticket records the relationship to `moldavite-evasive-elephant` and `royal-weariless-zebrafish`.\n\n## Fix Plan (Phase 2 — re-investigation; bound STAYS 30s, c2ba parity test untouched)\nRoot cause (RCA comment): on git >=2.47 the lock-held `git commit` runs `git maintenance run --auto` FOREGROUND (ADR 0051), so an O(store) repack is charged to `event_commit_git._GIT_TIMEOUT=30`; on a mature store it exceeds 30s and the commit is SIGKILLed (lost write + mid-repack corruption hazard). Fix decouples maintenance from the latency-bounded commit:\n- `gitutil.run_auto_maintenance(tracker)`: explicit `git maintenance run --auto` bounded by watchdog-grade `_LOCAL_GIT_TIMEOUT` (not the per-commit bound); best-effort; plus an `_AUTOMAINT_OFF` tuple (`-c gc.auto=0 -c maintenance.auto=false`).\n- `event_commit_git._git_commit`/`_git_commit_paths`: inject `_AUTOMAINT_OFF` so the 30s covers only the commit.\n- `event_append`: after a successful lock-held commit, call `run_auto_maintenance` UNDER the write lock (ADR 0051 serialization preserved; loose-growth still bounded).\n- `txn.py` (parity sibling): same maint-suppression + explicit post-commit maintenance for the claim/transition commit.\n- Regression test: with a store past the loose threshold and `_GIT_TIMEOUT` monkeypatched small, the write SUCCEEDS after the fix and FAILS (\"git timed out\") before it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (updated)\n- [x] Root cause demonstrated with repeatable evidence (RCA comment).\n- [ ] A regression test fails for the confirmed mechanism before the fix.\n- [ ] The fix addresses the failure class (both lock-held commit surfaces), not one run.\n- [ ] Focused store and lifecycle tests pass.\n- [x] Records the relationship to moldavite-evasive-elephant and royal-weariless-zebrafish."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787957350388389001,"uuid":"cbe3c2be-7ee8-446a-b690-430ccd44cc82"}